## 3. Cross-Contract Reentrancy

Attacker uses an **external contract** as intermediary.

```solidity
// Protocol A calls Protocol B which calls back to Protocol A

// VULNERABLE SCENARIO:
contract ProtocolA {
    IProtocolB public protocolB;
    
    function action() external {
        uint256 price = protocolB.getPrice();  // Calls external contract
        // Attacker contract as ProtocolB calls back!
        // ... uses stale state
    }
}
```

### Real Example: Curve Read-Only Reentrancy

```solidity
// Curve pool's get_virtual_price() can be called during reentrancy
// between remove_liquidity and callback, returning wrong price

interface ICurve {
    function get_virtual_price() external view returns (uint256);
    function remove_liquidity(uint256 amount) external;
}

// VULNERABLE: Using Curve price in callback
contract Vulnerable {
    ICurve curve;
    
    function action() external {
        uint256 price = curve.get_virtual_price();  // Stale during reentrancy!
        // ... use price
    }
}
```

