## 4. Read-Only Reentrancy

View functions return stale data during reentrant calls.

```solidity
// VULNERABLE - price oracle using pool reserves
contract VulnerableOracle {
    IPool pool;
    
    function getPrice() external view returns (uint256) {
        // During remove_liquidity callback, reserves are stale
        return pool.reserve0() * 1e18 / pool.reserve1();
    }
}

// ATTACK:
// 1. Call pool.remove_liquidity()
// 2. In callback, oracle.getPrice() returns pre-removal price
// 3. Borrow/trade at wrong price
// 4. Complete removal, price drops
```

### Mitigation: Check for Ongoing Operations

```solidity
// Some protocols expose reentrancy locks
interface IPool {
    function locked() external view returns (bool);
}

contract SecureOracle {
    function getPrice() external view returns (uint256) {
        require(!pool.locked(), "Pool locked");
        return pool.reserve0() * 1e18 / pool.reserve1();
    }
}
```

